==English==

===Etymology===
{{cal|en|la|[[nolō]] [[contendere]]||I don't want to contest}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|US|law}} A [[plea]] in a criminal case which means that the defendant admits no guilt but is no longer [[contest]]ing the charges brought against him/her.
#: {{syn|en|nolo contendere}}
# {{lb|en|US|law}} A [[clause]] in a [[will]] that [[impose]]s a [[penalty]] of [[forfeiture]] against any [[beneficiary]] who [[challenge]]s the will.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2021| title=A California Companion for the Course in Wills, Trusts, and Estates|author=Susan F. French | page=| passage='''No contest''' clauses are valid in California and are favored by the public policies of discouraging litigation and giving effect to the settlor's expressed purposes. }}
# {{lb|en|boxing|historic}} The result of a boxing [[bout]], [[promote]]d as an [[exhibition]] when the [[sport]] of boxing was [[illegal]], when a [[knockout]] did not occur.
# {{lb|en|boxing}} A bout that the [[referee]] [[cancel]]s early, either due to a [[serious]] [[injury]] early in the fight or due to a lack of [[action]]
# An [[election]] in which the [[candidate]] runs [[unopposed]].

===Interjection===
{{head|en|interjection}} {{lb|en|informal}}

{{rfquote-sense|en}}
# {{non-gloss definition|Used to indicate that a [[competition]] or [[comparison]] is [[one-sided]] and so its outcome is too [[obvious]] to be interesting.}}
# {{lb|en|emphatic}} {{non-gloss definition|Expresses lack of doubt (i.e., certainty) in a choice between options or preferences.}}
#: {{ux|en|I'll take a Porsche, '''no contest'''!}}
#: {{syn|en|no doubt}}<!--but not interchangeable-->

===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase}}

# {{ng|Indicates the perceived lack of any real competition because the “winner” or superior choice is obvious.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Peter M. Nichols|date=2000-11-05|title=HOLIDAY FILMS; Studios Move Slowly With DVD Boxed Sets|journal=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2000/11/05/movies/holiday-films-studios-move-slowly-with-dvd-boxed-sets.html#:~:text=In%20looks%20alone%20there%20is%20no%20contest.%20|text=To all the things DVD does better than the videocassette, add the boxed set. In looks alone there is '''no contest'''.}}

